DWORD dwRet = IsAccessAllowed(...); 
if (dwRet == ERROR) { 
// Security check failed. 
// Inform user that access is denied. 
} else { 
// Security check OK. 
} 
a. Explain the security flaw in this program. 
The above code allows access to a resource as long as dwRet is not an error. This is a clear flaw 
because there may be warnings, access denied, connection error or even invalid requests that 
are returned by dwRet that the above code does not check for. 
b. Rewrite the code to avoid the flaw (Hint: Consider the design principle of fail-safe defaults.) 

DWORD dwRet = IsAccessAllowed(…); 
if (dwRet == ACCESS_GRANTED){ 

// Security check OK. 
} else { 

// Security check failed. 

// Inform user that access is denied. 
}
